    "lawCode": "Amd §11, Transp Corps L",
    "lawSection": "Transportation Corporations Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7391\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the transportation corporation law, in relation to the\npowers of gas and electric corporations\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo limit efforts to use eminent domain to public purposes.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISION:\nProvides that (1) electric corporations that seek, through themselves\nor through one or more affiliated interests, to build or expand\ntransmission lines connecting a location outside the territorial\nlimits of the United States to a location within the State of New York\nor (2) electric corporations seeking to build or expand an electric\nfacility outside the United States and inter-connecting to a location\nwithin the State, shall not be afforded the power of eminent domain.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe power of eminent domain should be used to achieve public purposes\nthat inure to the benefit of the State. Transmission and generation\nprojects that originate outside the territorial limits of the United\nStates do not sufficiently benefit New York State and do not\nsufficiently encourage employment opportunities or economic\ndevelopment within the State.  Such projects will (1) discourage\nrepowering of existing generating facilities within the State, (2)\ndiscourage the rebuilding of existing transmission lines in the State,\nand (3) discourage the building of new transmission lines and\ngenerating facilities, including renewable resources, within the\nState. Construction and development of these facilities and\ninfrastructure in New York State, rather than outside the country,\nmaximizes employment and economic development in New York State and in\nour nation. Furthermore, by importing power from outside the United\nStates, our nation's dependency on foreign imports of energy is\nincreased.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
